# THE CLOCKWORK MOON
# A branching, three-act fairytale written entirely in external .vn files.
# 3 trail choices x 4 trials x 3 final choices = 36 completed playthroughs.
# Only built-in Vesper syntax is used; no Lua, Rust story code or new runtime APIs.

@scene threshold
set kindness = 0
set courage = 0
set starlight = 0
set pledge = false
set road = "unknown"
background cottage
music hearth
show tess curious at center
"Once upon a time, the moon above Bramblewick stopped turning. Its silver clockwork had caught on a thread of forgotten wishes."
"The baker's daughter Tess noticed first: the shadows stood still, the owls forgot their bedtime, and every puddle reflected the very same star."
tess: "If the moon cannot move, morning may never arrive. There must be something I can do."
sound bell
"On her windowsill lay a copper key, a fold of blue ribbon, and a note written in very small handwriting."
"The note said: Every brave heart must choose where to begin. The moon needs more than a key."
tess: "The lantern is ready. Which path shall I try?"
* "Follow the wandering firefly into the forest." -> firefly_trail
* "Listen for the singing river." -> river_trail
* "Ask the old owl for directions." -> owl_trail

@scene firefly_trail
set road = "firefly"
set starlight += 1
background forest
show wisp glowing at right
"The forest was full of blue shadows, but a tiny firefly stitched golden dots through the dark."
wisp: "Follow the light that does not hurry. A clock is not mended by chasing its hands."
tess: "That sounds like advice from someone who has already been lost."
if road == "firefly"
"The firefly flashed once for yes and twice for a very polite maybe."
end
sound sparkle
show tess determined at center
"The firefly left one bright spark in Tess's lantern, then slipped under a fern."
hide wisp
jump clearing

@scene river_trail
set road = "river"
set starlight += 2
background river
music wandering
"The river carried the reflection of a motionless moon, broken into a thousand patient pieces."
tess: "Do you know how to make the sky turn again?"
"The current answered with a melody. Tess understood only its last three notes, but they were enough to teach her how to listen."
if starlight >= 2
"She caught two silver droplets in her lantern. They shone without making the glass wet."
end
sound ripple
show tess curious at left
"Across the stepping stones, an owl waited beside a tree shaped like a crooked question mark."
jump clearing

@scene owl_trail
set road = "owl"
set courage += 1
background forest
show owl calm at left
owl: "The moon has forgotten a promise. The clock will not open until someone remembers it."
tess: "Then I shall ask every star what it remembers!"
owl: "A good plan, though stars tend to talk for a very long time."
if courage < 2
"Before leaving, the owl taught Tess a trick for being frightened: give fear a name, and it becomes a little easier to carry."
end
sound bell
hide owl
jump clearing

@scene clearing
background glade
music wandering
show owl calm at left
show tess curious at right
"In a clearing stood a wooden sign with four painted pictures: a bridge, a tower, a flower, and an ear."
owl: "One task will teach you the part of the promise you have forgotten. Choose carefully, but do not fear a kind mistake."
if starlight >= 2
"The droplets from the river hummed together, eager to become part of something useful."
else
"The lantern held only a little glow. Tess tightened the ribbon around its handle."
end
if courage != 0
"Tess remembered the owl's lesson and stood a little taller."
end
tess: "Very well. The moon shall have a story to tell when it wakes."
* "Repair the broken bridge." -> bridge_trial
* "Climb the clockkeeper's watchtower." -> tower_trial
* "Collect the sleeping moonflowers." -> flower_trial
* "Listen to what the owl has not yet said." -> listening_trial

@scene bridge_trial
background river
show tess determined at center
hide owl
"The little bridge had lost three boards. Underneath it, the river sang a song about people who could not cross."
tess: "I cannot fix the world tonight. But perhaps I can fix three boards."
set kindness += 2
sound knock
"She fitted the boards together and tied them with her blue ribbon, making room for a hedgehog family to cross."
if kindness > 1
"The hedgehogs bowed so deeply that their noses brushed the planks."
end
tess: "A bridge is a promise that the other side is worth reaching."
jump moon_gate

@scene tower_trial
background tower
show tess determined at right
hide owl
"The watchtower spiraled so high that even its stairs appeared to be tired."
set courage += 2
tess: "One step, then another. A great journey is only many small journeys keeping each other company."
sound knock
"At the top she found a brass wheel. It would not turn until she spoke her fear aloud."
tess: "I am afraid I will fail. I will help anyway."
if courage >= 2
"At once the wheel moved a single notch, and a faraway bell answered."
end
jump moon_gate

@scene flower_trial
background glade
show tess curious at center
"The moonflowers slept under a blanket of mist, their white petals curled like letters no one had opened."
set starlight += 1
set courage -= 1
tess: "I shall borrow only the light they can spare."
sound sparkle
"She touched the ground beside each flower rather than plucking it. A few gentle sparks rose into her lantern."
if starlight <= 1
"The lantern glimmered faintly, and Tess realized that even a small beginning counted."
else
"The light spread across the glass in tiny constellations."
end
jump moon_gate

@scene listening_trial
background glade
show owl calm at left
set kindness += 1
set pledge = true
owl: "Listen: the moon did not stop because its gears were broken. It stopped because no one remembered to wish goodnight to the lonely stars."
tess: "Then the promise is simple. We must remember even those we cannot see."
"Buenas noches, estrellas. Goodnight, stars. おやすみ、月."
if pledge == true
"The owl blinked, which is how an owl applauds when it is trying to seem dignified."
end
sound bell
jump moon_gate

@scene moon_gate
background gate
music hearth
show owl calm at right
show tess determined at center
"At the edge of the sleeping sky stood the Clockwork Gate. Its keyhole was shaped like a question, and its hinges were made of gentle thunder."
"The gate asked what Tess had brought from the road. It did not seem interested in her shoes, her name, or whether she was important."
if pledge == true
"The blue ribbon stirred. Tess remembered that promises did not have to be grand to be kept."
else
"The copper key felt surprisingly heavy in Tess's hand."
end
if starlight >= 3
"The lantern held more light than she could count, but it still weighed almost nothing."
else
"Only a little starlight remained. Tess held it carefully."
end
if road != "unknown"
"The path behind Tess glimmered, remembering each step that had carried her here."
end
owl: "You may tell the truth, offer what you gathered, or go home with a promise you can keep. None is an unworthy answer."
* "Tell the gate the truth, even if it sounds foolish." -> speak_truth
* "Give the gate every spark of starlight." -> offer_light
* "Return home to share the story." -> go_home

@scene speak_truth
set courage += 1
set pledge = true
sound bell
tess: "The truth is that I am small, and I do not know how to mend the moon. But I am here, and I will not leave a frightened star alone."
"The gate sighed with relief, as though a secret had finally found its proper home."
jump judgement

@scene offer_light
set starlight += 1
sound sparkle
"The lantern opened like a flower. Out floated every spark Tess had saved, rising slowly toward the frozen moon."
if starlight >= 3
"The sky brightened from violet to silver as the sparks found their forgotten places."
else
"Only one or two sparks rose, but the moon welcomed them as if they were a thousand."
end
tess: "Take what I can give. It is enough to begin."
jump judgement

@scene go_home
set kindness += 1
hide owl
show tess relieved at center
"The gate did not lock when Tess turned away. Instead, it opened onto a path of familiar windows and warm kitchen lights."
tess: "A promise can start at home. Tomorrow we will remember the stars together."
jump ending_home

@scene judgement
background sky
hide owl
show tess relieved at center
music dawn
"The moon's great hands twitched. For an instant the whole sky seemed to hold its breath."
if kindness >= 2
jump ending_kind
else
if courage > 1
jump ending_bold
else
jump ending_quiet
end
end

@scene ending_kind
sound chime
"The repaired bridge became a silver line across the sky, and the moon followed it back into motion."
tess: "Maybe that is all kindness is: a bridge we make for someone else."
"The stars took turns twinkling so that even the shyest among them would be noticed."
"By morning, every clock in Bramblewick was running again. A hedgehog family sent Tess a note that said THANK YOU."
"The moon had kept its promise. And Tess knew she would keep hers."
"The End."

@scene ending_bold
sound chime
"The brass wheel at the top of the tower turned, one brave notch after another, until the moon's hands began to move."
tess: "I was scared the whole time. I suppose courage does not mean waiting until fear goes away."
"The first pale sunrise crept over the roofs. In every window, someone looked up and remembered to smile at the stars."
"The owl would later claim he had never doubted Tess for a moment. No one entirely believed him."
"The moon had kept its promise. And Tess knew she would keep hers."
"The End."

@scene ending_quiet
sound chime
"The clockwork moon listened to the tiniest spark, the softest promise, and the sound of a child choosing to try."
tess: "Even when I have very little light, I can still carry it."
"Then the great silver hands began to turn, quietly enough that only the owl noticed."
"At sunrise, Tess put the copper key on her windowsill for the next traveler who might need it."
"The moon had kept its promise. And Tess knew she would keep hers."
"The End."

@scene ending_home
background cottage
music dawn
show tess relieved at center
sound chime
"Tess returned to Bramblewick and told the baker, the tailor, the miller, and even the shy little mice about the lonely stars."
"That evening every window held a candle, and every voice made a little room for someone far away."
tess: "Buenas noches, estrellas. We have not forgotten you."
"The clockwork moon heard them all. Before the last candle went out, its great hands turned once more."
"Morning finally arrived, and with it the smell of fresh bread."
"The End."
